<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Amundsen returns six weeks after starting duloxetine; he has taken 60 mg daily for five weeks. The mild nausea of the first days has gone, and he has had no drowsiness, dizziness or sweating. His average finger pain over the past week is 3 of 10; the cold attacks are shorter and less frequent, though the spring weather is milder too. He sleeps through most nights. He uses capsaicin cream only on cold days. He can manage buttons and keys outdoors with liner gloves. He did not have the blood test that was meant to be done two to four weeks after starting duloxetine. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Finger pain</td><td>Average 3 of 10 over the past week</td></tr><tr><td>Medicine effects</td><td>Early nausea gone; no drowsiness, dizziness or sweating</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Sleeping through most nights</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Manages buttons and keys outdoors with liner gloves</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

